{"content":[{"c":["MEMUCAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of the seven princes of Persia and Media under King Ahasuerus (",{"href":"?bref=Esth.1.14-21","r":"Esth.1.14-21","rawR":"Esth.1.14-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.1.14-21","value":"Esth.1.14-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Est 1:14-21"},"). He brought charges against Vashti, the Persian queen, who had refused to make a royal appearance that the king had commanded (v ",{"href":"?bref=Esth.1.16","r":"Esth.1.16","rawR":"Esth.1.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.1.16","value":"Esth.1.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"16"},"). Memucan proposed that she be divested of her position and the queenship given to another; the king took his counsel and issued a decree to that effect (v ",{"href":"?bref=Esth.1.21","r":"Esth.1.21","rawR":"Esth.1.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.1.21","value":"Esth.1.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"21"},"). Hence Esther was chosen as queen over Media and Persia."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Memucan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Est 1:14-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Esth.1.14-21","rawQueryValue":"Esth.1.14-21","sourceRefExact":"Esth.1.14-21"},{"anchorText":"16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Esth.1.16","rawQueryValue":"Esth.1.16","sourceRefExact":"Esth.1.16"},{"anchorText":"21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Esth.1.21","rawQueryValue":"Esth.1.21","sourceRefExact":"Esth.1.21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6e17b11afff6bf43e24619f753bdd76d872f4f18d25024b26c2b1c50c3861db2","sourceItemName":"Memucan","sourceItemOrder":236,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Memucan","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitle